1. THE ACCEPTANCE GATE — the three named e2e tests, test file UNMODIFIED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Command:
  pytest packages/ai-parrot/tests/integration/test_finance_reporter_narrative_e2e.py -v

Result (first attempt, BEFORE the renderer-text-omission fix below):
  test_report_profile_replay_no_narrator          FAILED
  test_dashboard_profile_replay                   PASSED
  test_end_to_end_no_fabricated_figures            FAILED
  8 passed, 2 failed

  test_dashboard_profile_replay passing alone is NOT evidence the feature
  works (per spec Known Risks) — it only exercises the INTERCEPTED
  Infographic path, fixed by TASK-2753 alone. The two LOWERED-path
  failures were a genuine gap: baking correctly drops the "text" key for
  an omitted optional binding (TASK-2754's propagation made this
  possible), but interactive_html.py's `_render_prim_Text` /
  ssr_html.py's `_render_Text` unconditionally emitted the wrapping
  `<p class="a2ui-...">` regardless of whether "text" was present, so an
  omitted /narrative binding still leaked a visible-but-blank
  `a2ui-body`/`a2ui-summary` element into the document — failing
  `assert "a2ui-body" not in html_doc`.

  FIX (completes TASK-2753/2754's own files — interactive_html.py /
  ssr_html.py — no other files touched): both `_render_prim_Text` and
  `_render_Text` now omit the whole element (return "") when the "text"
  key is entirely absent from the baked props (the omitted-optional-
  binding signal), matching the precedent already established by
  `_render_infographic`'s `if text is not None` guard. SSRHTMLRenderer's
  version additionally excludes `role == "cell"` (a DataTable cell's own
  value is never itself an optional binding; omitting it would misalign
  the row).

